# MeloScore Privacy Policy

**Last updated: 6 November 2026**

MeloScore is a music notation application developed by Phil Blandford. This policy explains how personal information is collected, used and protected when you use MeloScore.

## 1. Information We Collect

Depending on the features you use, MeloScore may process:

- **Account information:** Your name, email address and account identifier when you sign in using a supported authentication provider.
- **Musical scores:** Scores you create, import or edit, stored locally on your device or on our servers when you use cloud storage or synchronisation.
- **Technical information:** Device characteristics, application version, diagnostic information and error reports.
- **Usage analytics:** When enabled, information about application usage, feature interactions, performance and errors, stored using Google Cloud Firestore.
- **Optional score quality-control data:** Musical scores you explicitly agree to share with the developer for testing and improving notation quality.

## 2. How We Use Your Information

We process information to:

- Authenticate users and manage accounts.
- Store and synchronise musical scores.
- Provide access to licensed features.
- Diagnose errors and improve reliability.
- Understand application usage and performance.
- Investigate notation and engraving problems where users have explicitly consented.

We do not sell personal information or use it for targeted advertising.

## 3. Optional Score Quality-Control Programme

MeloScore may offer an optional programme allowing users to contribute musical scores for quality improvement.

Participation is voluntary and is not required to use the application.

When the programme is available:

- Users will be asked for explicit consent before their scores are contributed.
- Contributed scores may be inspected by the developer to identify notation errors, layout defects and other problems.
- Scores will not be published, sold or shared with other users as part of this programme.
- Users may withdraw their consent at any time.
- Withdrawal will stop further collection under the programme. Previously contributed scores will be deleted where applicable, subject to lawful retention requirements explained to the user.

Scores stored for synchronisation are not automatically made available for developer quality-control inspection.

## 4. Analytics and Diagnostics

MeloScore plans to use Google Cloud Firestore to store application usage and diagnostic events.

These events may include application version, device characteristics, feature usage, performance measurements and error information.

Analytics are intended to help improve application reliability and usability, not to identify users for advertising purposes.

Musical score content will not be included in analytics events unless the user has separately consented to sharing scores for quality control.

## 5. Storage and International Data Transfers

MeloScore's application server and primary database are hosted on a Vultr virtual private server located in New Jersey, United States.

Account information and musical scores stored through MeloScore's cloud services are processed on this server.

Usage analytics, when introduced, will be stored separately using Google Cloud Firestore. The location of that data will depend on the configured Firestore database region.

We use encrypted network connections and access controls to protect information.

Where personal information is transferred outside the United Kingdom or European Economic Area, we will use applicable legal safeguards as required by data protection law.

## 6. Third-Party Services

MeloScore uses or may use:

- **Vultr:** Application hosting and primary database infrastructure.
- **Google:** Authentication and, when introduced, Cloud Firestore analytics storage.
- **Apple:** Application distribution and associated platform services.

We do not sell personal information to third parties.

## 7. Sharing of Information

We do not sell or rent personal information.

Information may be shared with service providers where necessary to operate MeloScore or where required by law.

Musical scores are not made public unless users explicitly choose to share or publish them through an available feature.

## 8. Children's Privacy and Educational Use

MeloScore may be used in educational settings.

We aim to minimise the personal information collected from pupils and other users and do not use children's personal information for targeted advertising.

The optional score quality-control programme will not be enabled for school-managed accounts unless appropriate consent and institutional arrangements have been established.

## 9. Data Retention and Deletion

Personal information is retained only as long as necessary for the purposes described in this policy, subject to applicable legal obligations.

Users may request deletion of their accounts and associated personal information by contacting the developer.

Users who have contributed scores for quality control may withdraw their consent and request deletion of previously contributed scores.

## 10. Your Rights

Depending on applicable law, users may have rights to access, correct, export, restrict processing of or request deletion of personal information.

UK and European users may also have rights to object to certain processing and complain to the relevant data protection authority.

## 11. Changes to This Policy

We may update this policy as MeloScore develops. Material changes will be communicated where required by law.

